      "description": "Watch Ferencváros vs Twente highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 30, 2026. The UEFA Europa League provided a spectacle of high drama on 2026-07-30 as Ferencváros hosted Twente in a clash defined by tactical shifts and unexpected disciplinary turns. Fans at the stadium witnessed a game of two halves where momentum proved to be a fickle friend for both sides. Early Dominance and Red Card Chaos The match ignited in the 22nd minute when Ferencváros were awarded a penalty. Toon Raemaekers stepped up to the spot and, with clinical composure, converted the chance to give the home side an early lead. However, the atmosphere shifted drastically in the 33rd minute. Philippe Rommens was shown a straight red card, sparking heavy protests from his teammates and leaving the hosts to navigate the majority of the contest with only ten men. Defying the Odds and the Twente Fightback Despite the numerical disadvantage, the hosts started the second half with renewed energy. In the 50th minute, Lenny Joseph doubled the advantage, finishing a well-placed pass from Kristoffer Zachariassen . It seemed Ferencváros might pull off a miraculous victory against the odds. As the clock ticked down, Twente manager introduced Marko Pjaca and Lucas Vennegoor of Hesselink to exploit the tiring home defense. The tactical changes paid dividends in a frantic closing period. In the 83rd minute, Wout Weghorst pulled one back for the visitors after being set up by Pjaca . The momentum had swung completely, and just three minutes later, the comeback was complete. Lucas Vennegoor of Hesselink found the back of the net following a delivery from Bart van Rooij , silencing the home crowd and securing a dramatic 2-2 draw. Late yellow cards for Thomas van den Belt and Younes Taha underlined the physical nature of a contest that neither side was willing to lose."
